@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+---
+type: adr
+status: draft
+entities: [Comment, CommentReport]
+related:
+  - app/Http/Controllers/CommentController.ts
+  - app/Http/Controllers/PostController.ts
+  - app/Http/Resources/CommentResource.ts
+  - app/Policies/CommentPolicy.ts
+  - db/schema.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-code/claude-fable-5-1", at: 2026-09-29T13:47:59.141Z }
+---
+
+# Hide reported comments and delete them with their post
+
+## Context
+
+Readers can comment on posts, and nobody moderates them: the community has
+to keep the comments clean. Reported comments must stay in the database for
+a review screen that does not exist yet, and the tooling for it reads the
+`comments` and `comment_reports` tables directly, without the ORM.
+
+## Decision
+
+- **Hiding is derived, not stored.** A comment is hidden once
+  `REPORTS_TO_HIDE` (3) different users reported it (`Comment.isHidden()`).
+  `PostController.show` leaves hidden comments out for every viewer, the
+  comment's author and the post's author included. There is no `hidden`
+  column to fall out of step with the reports.
+- **One report per user per comment**, held by the unique index on
+  (`comment_id`, `user_id`). Reporting again answers 204 and writes nothing.
+  Anyone signed in can report, the comment's own author included.
+- **Deleting is a hard delete**, allowed to the comment's author and the
+  author of the post it is on (`CommentPolicy.delete`). Being hidden does not
+  change who may delete a comment.
+- **Rows that go with a post or a comment are deleted by hand**, in one
+  transaction, children first. The foreign keys declare `ON DELETE CASCADE`
+  as well, but SQLite only enforces foreign keys on a connection that turned
+  them on, and the app's connection does not.
+- **`created_at` is a column default** on the two tables (the same ISO 8601
+  shape the other tables get from `$defaultFn`), so a row written without
+  the ORM is still complete.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The post page loads the reports of every comment on it to decide what to
+  show. That is bounded by comments × reporters; if it grows, move the rule
+  into the query as a grouped count.
+- A comment's author can delete their comment after it was hidden, which
+  takes it away from the later review. Blocking that is a product decision
+  this ticket did not make.
+- Changing the threshold is a one-line change to `REPORTS_TO_HIDE` and
+  applies to existing comments at once, in both directions.
